  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \nThe new approach combines Differential Evolution (DE) for global exploration and Quadratic Programming (QP) for local refinement to minimize C\u2085. DE rapidly explores the solution space, while QP refines candidates using convex relaxations, addressing GA's limitations on the previous 0.381005 solution.\n\n2. Mathematical specification  \nDefine the problem as minimax optimization over h \u2208 [0,1]^n, sum(h) = n/2. The overlap integral at shift k is:\n\n$$C(k) = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} h[i](1 - h[(i+k)\\mod n])$$\n\nObjective: minimize $$C\u2085 = \\max_k |C(k)|$$\n\nQP relaxation:  \nMinimize C using auxiliary variables w_ij = h[i]h[j], subject to 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 and sum(h) = n/2.\n\n3. Implementation procedure  \n1. **Validation of initial_h_values**: Check feasibility (sum=1, bounds).  \n2. **DE Initialization**:  \n   - Population size 50.  \n   - Initialize with initial_h_values scaled to [0,1] and sum=1.  \n3. **DE Mutation**:  \n   - v_j = x_i + F*(x_r1 - x_r2) with F=0.7.  \n4. **DE Crossover**:  \n   - u_j = x_i + CR*(v_j - x_i), CR=0.9.  \n5. **Selection**: Keep individuals with lower C\u2085.  \n6. **QP Refinement**:  \n   - Take top 10 candidates.  \n   - Solve for h in relaxed QP formulation.  \n   - Project back to [0,1] and normalize.  \n7. **Termination**: Stop at 950s, return best.\n\n4. Search choices  \n- Population size 50.  \n- Mutation: F=0.7, CR=0.9.  \n- QP steps: every 50 DE iterations.  \n- Refinement: top 10% candidates.  \n\n5. Compute budget  \n- DE: 500s for 1000 generations.  \n- QP: 300s for 100 refinements.  \n- Total: 800s + 300s validation = 1100s.  \n\n6. Validation and return contract  \n- Verify \u222bh=1 and 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1.  \n- Recompute C\u2085 with evaluator.  \n- Return initial_h_values if no improvement.",
